  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong reference point by testing the most complete multimodal configuration. config_039 combines all the most expressive components: multimodal fusion (leveraging both RNA and image), multiprofile (richer cellular representation), scgpt (learned context-aware RNA encoder), imagenet_vit_l (strong pretrained vision encoder), transformer aggregation (most flexible multi-profile combination), and weighted fusion (learned modality balancing). This tests whether the full pipeline yields high validation accuracy, giving me a strong baseline to compare against. In subsequent experiments, I can systematically ablate individual components (e.g., swap scgpt→pca, imagenet_vit_l→resnet50, transformer→avgpool, or drop to single-modality) to identify which design choices drive performance. Starting here maximizes information gain per experiment under the 10-run budget."
